-- title:
--   One step of Gotzmann's persistence theorem
-- statement:
--   Let $n, m$ be natural numbers, $K$ a field, and $J$ an ideal of the polynomial ring $K[X_0,\dots,X_n]$ in $n+1$ variables. Assume $J$ is generated by forms of degree $m$: there is a set $s$ of polynomials, each homogeneous of degree $m$, with $J = \mathrm{span}\,s$. For a natural number $d$, `piece J d` denotes the degree-$d$ graded piece of the quotient, namely the $K$-module of homogeneous polynomials of degree $d$ modulo those of them lying in $J$, and $\mathrm{macaulayPow}\,d\,a$ is Macaulay's upper pseudo-power $a^{\langle d\rangle}$, given recursively by $a^{\langle 0\rangle}=0$ and, with $k$ the greatest $k \le a+d+1$ such that $\binom{k}{d+1}\le a$, by $a^{\langle d+1\rangle} = \binom{k+1}{d+2} + \bigl(a-\binom{k}{d+1}\bigr)^{\langle d\rangle}$. Assume that the growth from degree $m$ to degree $m+1$ is maximal, i.e. $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,(m+1) = \bigl(\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,m\bigr)^{\langle m\rangle}$. The conclusion is that the next growth is again maximal: $\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,(m+2) = \bigl(\dim_K \mathrm{piece}\,J\,(m+1)\bigr)^{\langle m+1\rangle}$.
--
--   This is the inductive step of Gotzmann's persistence theorem: for an ideal generated in a single degree $m$, maximal Macaulay growth of the Hilbert function from degree $m$ to $m+1$ persists to the next degree. It is cited by [`MvPolynomial.finrank_piece_eq_of_maximal_growth`](thm.html#MvPolynomial.finrank_piece_eq_of_maximal_growth), which iterates it to obtain persistence in all degrees $e \ge m$, used in turn for the Hilbert functor of projective space.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_finrank_piece_add_two_eq_macaulayPow_of_finrank_piece_succ_eq_macaulayPow.lean

